  "slug": "generator-intake-form",
  "title": "Generator Intake Form",
  "subtitle": "An original generator workflow that turns an initial request into a triaged, evidence-backed assignment, with explicit qualified-review, stop-work, escalation, and accountable handoff controls.",
  "description": "A workflow-complete generator intake form for the standby or prime generator system that captures exact identity, domain observations, supporting evidence, decisions, exceptions, responsible owners, and closeout without replacing professional judgment or the organization's controlling procedures.",
  "use_case": "Use when a coordinator receives a new request and must verify identity, scope, evidence, hazards, feasibility, and the next accountable handoff before field activity is scheduled. The generator service coordinator owns routing, and closure requires documented evidence, disposition of restrictions, and acceptance by the designated reviewer.",
  "risk_tier": "B",
  "sections": [
